   "text": "I read the image as a lipidated, disulfide-cyclised peptide and wrote the SMILES residue by residue, from the lauroyl tail to the C-terminal amide.\n\n**Lipid tail and linkers**\n- Lauroyl (C12 acyl) is attached to the \u03b1-nitrogen of a \u03b3-linked L-Glu, which keeps its free \u03b1-COOH.\n- The Glu side chain is linked through two 2-(2-aminoethoxy)ethoxyacetyl (AEEA) spacers to the N-terminus of the first penicillamine (Pen).\n\n**Cyclic part (disulfide between the two Pen residues)**\n- Pen1, then Asn, Thr, 7-methyl-Trp and N\u03b5-acetyl-Lys, then Pen2.\n- The two Pen CMe\u2082 sulfurs are joined by the S\u2013S bond, closing the macrocycle.\n\n**Tail beyond Pen2**\n- Tyr with its phenol O-alkylated by CH\u2082CH\u2082\u2013NH\u2013C(=NH)NH\u2082 (a guanidinoethyl ether).\n- 2-Naphthylalanine.\n- 4-Aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid, which has no stereocentre.\n- Glu with a free side-chain COOH.\n- Asn.\n- 3-Pyridylalanine.\n- C-terminal N-methylglycinamide (sarcosinamide), N(CH\u2083)CH\u2082C(=O)NH\u2082.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- Wedge and hash bonds are hard to resolve at several centres. I assumed natural L configuration for Glu, Asn, Thr, Trp, Lys, Tyr, 2-Nal and 3-Pal.\n- By my reading of the drawing, Pen1 is L (R) and Pen2 is D (S). These two assignments are the least certain.\n\nSMILES: CCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)NCCOCCOCC(=O)NCCOCCOCC(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCNC(=N)N)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O)C(C)(C)SSC1(C)C)C(=O)O"
